    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2MW4GjSnr3iyBBgNjs3QkTQ)_\n\n## What\n\n- `- seealso :: [[id:...]]` meta lines (Vulpea) are now a source of mentions in `sp-see-also`, like the `* See also` heading from #388.\n- Key matched in any case, any spacing; the `-`/`+` bullet is optional.\n- Each `id:` link on the line is one mention with `:where` `section` (weight 1.5), so it shows up in `sp-see-also-show`, the widgets, the `concept-usage` block and `*see-also-concept*`.\n- Section-level, not granular: the mention belongs to the heading the line is in (nearest ID'd heading, or the file before the first heading).\n- Not counted: lines in source/example/comment blocks, `#`-commented lines, and lines inside a `See also` section (read once, there).\n\n## How\n\n- Link scanning of the `See also` code path moved into `sp-see-also--link-items`, shared with the new `sp-see-also--meta-items`.\n- Cache version 3 → 4 so cached files are re-read.\n- Literate source `docs/tangles/academic/sp-see-also.org` updated (module and tests are tangled from it), with a new bullet-list section.\n- No `CHANGELOG.org` edit.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 4 new ERT tests; all 32 sp-see-also tests pass in Emacs 29.3.\n- Not run on the real vault or in the GUI.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAuWUsM6NcefGcZoh9)_",
